# The build context is the repository root, so everything not excluded here is uploaded to the
# daemon on every build — twice, because there are two images.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters: it is a tree of symlinks into a hidden store, it does not
# survive the trip, and both images install or skip dependencies themselves.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The dev stack's state and this worktree's derived configuration. `.env*` in particular: a build
# context carrying a real key bakes it into a layer.
.env
.env.*
.dev
.eait-slot
src/frontend/dist

# Nothing the running server reads.
.github
test-results
playwright-report
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store

# The deploy tree itself: the running server reads none of it. The two Dockerfiles are re-included
# because they live here — BuildKit reads the `-f` file from outside the context, the classic
# builder does not, and one negated line costs nothing.
src/iac
!src/iac/Dockerfile.backend
!src/iac/Dockerfile.frontend
